<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Derby</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Derby is a city in the East <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/midlands">Midlands</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> on the River Derwent. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viking-age">Viking Age</a> it was one of the Five Boroughs of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danelaw">Danelaw</a>, taken by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aethelflaed">Æthelflæd</a> of Mercia in 917. In the 18th century the Lombe brothers' <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silk">silk</a> mill made it an early centre of factory industry, part of the Derwent Valley Mills World Heritage Site, and it later became a base for railway and aero-engine manufacture.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/derby.jpg" alt="Derby" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: GR77 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Derby_Cathedral_at_night.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
